1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,870
740 jobs.

2
00:00:01,720 --> 00:00:03,480
68 applications.

3
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:04,560
12 interviews.

4
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:05,350
One offer.

5
00:00:05,330 --> 00:00:07,050
That's one guy's job hunt,

6
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:07,890
run by Claude.

7
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:09,140
And the smartest part?

8
00:00:08,990 --> 00:00:09,950
What it tells you

9
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,000
not to apply to.

10
00:00:11,030 --> 00:00:12,370
You paste a job link.

11
00:00:12,340 --> 00:00:13,520
It reads the job,

12
00:00:13,370 --> 00:00:14,310
and scores it

13
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:16,170
against your resume, 1 to 5.

14
00:00:16,020 --> 00:00:16,870
Below 4?

15
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:17,610
It tells you

16
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:18,300
to skip it.

17
00:00:18,150 --> 00:00:20,060
No more wasted applications.

18
00:00:19,910 --> 00:00:20,760
Above 4,

19
00:00:20,610 --> 00:00:22,220
it tailors your resume

20
00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:23,530
into a PDF screening

21
00:00:23,380 --> 00:00:24,470
software can read.

22
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:25,790
Writes the cover letter.

23
00:00:25,790 --> 00:00:27,080
Drafts an answer for

24
00:00:26,930 --> 00:00:28,270
every form field.

25
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:29,350
But here's the catch.

26
00:00:29,270 --> 00:00:30,670
It never hits submit.

27
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:31,460
You read it,

28
00:00:31,310 --> 00:00:32,290
and you send it.

29
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:33,740
It's called career-ops.

30
00:00:33,590 --> 00:00:35,980
77,000 GitHub stars.

31
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:37,350
Free, and open source.

32
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,420
Comment OFFER,

33
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:39,120
and I'll DM

34
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:39,800
you the repo,

35
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:40,980
plus my step-by-step

36
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:41,980
setup with Claude.

